<p>Port Arthur wind damage claims cover a wide range of losses: shingles peeled off a ridge by a thunderstorm gust, a pine limb through the roof, a metal shop building with panels pulled loose, or a fence flattened by a squall line. Wind is a covered peril on most property policies, but in Jefferson County it is often covered by a different policy than the rest of the home. Before you file, it helps to know which policy applies, which deductible applies, and how the insurer will decide whether wind actually caused the damage.</p>

<h2>Sources of Wind Damage in Southeast Texas</h2>
<p>Hurricanes get the attention, but much of the wind damage around Port Arthur happens on ordinary stormy afternoons.</p>
